# Exhaustive by policy (SITE-BRIEF § Chatbot ops). A variable that the code
# reads and this file does not name is a defect: the deploy is meant to fail
# loudly on a missing secret, and it cannot do that if nobody knows the secret
# exists. Nothing here has a value; values live in Vercel.

# --- Contact -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional server-only override used for local or staging QA.
# Production defaults to the shared Utlyze lead gateway.
LEAD_INGEST_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4011

# --- Ask dock ----------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ROUTE IS ALL-OR-NOTHING. It answers only when the key AND a rate-limit
# store are both present. With either one missing, GET/POST /api/ask answer 503
# {"state":"not_configured"} and the dock keeps its terms-and-mailto behaviour.
# There is no in-memory fallback for the limits: a process-local counter on a
# serverless platform is per instance, which is not a limit.

# xAI API key, server-only. Never exposed to the browser, never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
XAI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to the model pinned in lib/ask/limits.ts (BUILD-VERIFIED
# 2026-08-11: grok-4.5). Set it only to move deliberately, and update the
# pricing constants in the same commit or the spend ceiling stops being true.
XAI_MODEL=

# The rate-limit and spend store. EITHER pair is enough; both speak the same
# REST protocol. Upstash Redis:
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# …or Vercel KV:
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Optional. Salts the hash of a visitor's IP before it becomes a counter key,
# so the store never holds an address. Falls back to the API key when unset.
ASK_IP_SALT=
